    class="sechead"
  >
    <h2>
      Recommended development
    </h2>
    <span
      class="desc"
    >
      Thisai programmes matched to this profile
    </span>
  </div>
  <div
    class="recgrid"
  >
    <div
      class="rec"
    >
      <span
        class="tag"
      >
        Practice tool
         · 
        Equity of Treatment
      </span>
      <b>
        Attention Audit
      </b>
      <p>
        A tally sheet and a 15-minute peer observation protocol that records only who you called on, who you followed up with, and who you let pass. The pattern is almost never the one teachers predict.
      </p>
      <div
        class="meta"
      >
        <span>
          2 weeks
        </span>
        <span>
          Self-paced + peer observer
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rec"
    >
      <span
        class="tag"
      >
        Practice tool
         · 
        Instructional Adaptability
      </span>
      <b>
        Mid-Lesson Checkpoints
      </b>
      <p>
        Two diagnostic questions at the fifteen-minute mark, and a decision rule for what to do with the answer. Turns adaptability from instinct into a scheduled habit.
      </p>
      <div
        class="meta"
      >
        <span>
          3 weeks
        </span>
        <span>
          Self-paced
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rec"
    >
      <span
        class="tag"
      >
        Micro-course
         · 
        Doubt-Resolution & Responsiveness
      </span>
      <b>
        The Second Explanation
      </b>
      <p>
        Builds a personal bank of second and third representations for the five concepts your learners most reliably get stuck on, so an explanation that does not land has somewhere to go.
      </p>
      <div
        class="meta"
      >
        <span>
          4 sessions
        </span>
        <span>
          Video + classroom task
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div
    class="sechead"
  >
    <h2>
      Six-week development path
    </h2>
    <span
      class="desc"
    >
      Sequenced from the two widest gaps
    </span>
  </div>
  <ol
    class="path"
    style="list-style: none; margin: 0px; padding: 0px;"
  >
    <li
      class="pstep"
    >
      <span
        class="wk"
      >
        Weeks 1–2
      </span>
      <div>
        <b>
          Attention Audit — Equity of Treatment
        </b>
        <p>
          A tally sheet and a 15-minute peer observation protocol that records only who you called on, who you followed up with, and who you let pass. The pattern is almost never the one teachers predict.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pstep"
    >
      <span
        class="wk"
      >
        Week 3
      </span>
      <div>
        <b>
          Peer observation, one focus only
        </b>
        <p>
          A colleague watches one lesson and records nothing except equity of treatment. Twenty minutes of debrief, no written record, not used for appraisal.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pstep"
    >
      <span
        class="wk"
      >
        Weeks 4–5
      </span>
      <div>
        <b>
          Mid-Lesson Checkpoints — Instructional Adaptability
        </b>
        <p>
          Two diagnostic questions at the fifteen-minute mark, and a decision rule for what to do with the answer. Turns adaptability from instinct into a scheduled habit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pstep"
    >
      <span
        class="wk"
      >
        Week 6
      </span>
      <div>
        <b>
          Reassess and compare
        </b>
        <p>
          The teacher retakes the reflection on the same grade band. The comparison worth reading is per dimension, not the index — a five-point index move can hide the only change that mattered.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li
      class="pstep"
    >
      <span
        class="wk"
      >
        Ongoing
      </span>
      <div>
        <b>
          Deploy their strength in Doubt-Resolution & Responsiveness
        </b>
        <p>
          Academic heads pair teachers on complementary profiles. This dimension is where this teacher would be most useful to a colleague, and mentoring is the fastest way to consolidate it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p
    class="foot-note"
  >
    The index summarises the seven dimension scores; it is not a rating and not comparable across grade bands, since each band draws on its own scenarios. School averages are computed only from teachers with a submitted profile, and shown only when at least five teachers are included. Scenarios are composites of documented classroom patterns rather than single cited studies; each item carries its own source note in the question bank.
  </p>
  <div
    class="expert"
  >
    <button
      aria-expanded="false"
    >
      <span
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="chev"
      >
        ▶
      </span>
       Item-level ranking data
      <span
        class="tag"
      >
        Admin only · 
        3
         items
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>
</main>
`;

